# Livepad

Self-hosted interview IDE. Interviewer has an account; candidate joins `/r/:slug?token=` with a display name only.

Stack: pnpm workspaces. `apps/web` Vite React Tailwind Monaco. `apps/api` Fastify better-auth Drizzle Hocuspocus. `apps/runner` Node jobs. Shared types in `packages/shared`.

Start: copy `.env.example` → `.env`, `pnpm install`, `pnpm db:up` (or `pnpm db:up:local` on Windows without Docker), `pnpm db:push`, `pnpm dev`. UI `localhost:5173`, API `3001`, collab WS `1234`, runner `4000`.

Vite proxies `/api`, `/ws`, and `/collab` (→ Hocuspocus `:1234`). Browser uses same-origin `/collab`; Hocuspocus still listens on `:1234` (see `apps/web/src/lib/collab-url.ts`).

## Do

- Put shared DTOs in `packages/shared`, then use them on web and api.
- Talk to the user in Russian. Keep UI copy in Russian.
- Tell the candidate if integrity signals are collected. Host-only panel.
- Prefer Docker runner; local node/npm is a Windows fallback with timeouts.

## Don't

- Don't add Piston. It cannot `npm install`; revisit only for Python/Java/C++ contests.
- Don't build covert tab/paste/monitor telemetry. Don't log clipboard text — length only.
- Don't add assignment pools, timers, autograde, chat, video, LSP, TTY, or Google login unless asked.
- Don't commit `.env` or `.tools/`. Don't invent secrets or test passwords in docs.

Read `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` for file map and verify steps.
